# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Avatar 90 fps base with frame generation x2 (180 fps displayed), -src 90, b:vsync present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit, passthrough threshold a quarter of the source period. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. The base cannot hold 90 here: real frames arrive at 88 per second with the batch period wandering around 11.1 ms, the M=2 comb engages a quarter of the time, and the phase wanders instead of alternating.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 90 fps base with frame generation x2 (180 fps displayed), -src 90, b:vsync present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit, passthrough threshold a quarter of the source period. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. The base cannot hold 90 here: real frames arrive at 88 per second with the batch period wandering around 11.1 ms, the M=2 comb engages a quarter of the time, and the phase wanders instead of alternating.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 5
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 45.2
src_hint 90.0
# min_placed_pct: 92.7% of captures anchored to a flip, 7.2% with no anchor. The source is a
# 180 Hz stream the base cannot hold (88 real frames a second, batch period wandering around
# 11.1 ms), so one capture in fourteen has no flip it can be placed on. A property of this
# source, not of the join; the steady 90x1 run anchors 99.5%.
min_placed_pct 92
# Replay 44.1% / runs 0 / worst 4 / re-seeds 0 against field 45.2% / runs 0 / worst 5. On the
# quarter-source-period threshold 99.5% of midpoint presents blend even though the comb engaged
# on only 23% of presents in this test: a wandering phase still lands inside a blend band that
# spans w in [0.31, 0.69]. Content steps are 1.5 periods on 84% of presents against 23% on the
# capture this replaced (present-period floor, 9.9% replay synth), with the remainder spread by
# the source's own wobble, not quantized to 1.0 / 2.0 pairs.
